9 @ _process()`\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3365682480/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3530222925","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109257#issuecomment-3530222925","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109257","id":3530222925,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Sau1N","user":{"login":"manosmiras","id":91184113,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMTg0MTEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91184113?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/manosmiras","html_url":"https://github.com/manosmiras","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manosmiras/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manosmiras/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manosmiras/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manosmiras/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manosmiras/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manosmiras/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manosmiras/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manosmiras/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manosmiras/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T23:53:39Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T17:18:39Z","body":"I'm also experiencing the same issue, after upgrading from 4.4.1 to 4.5.1, I've also not been able to reduce it to a MRP.\n\nThe error, in my case is coming from an `AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D`, it seems that giving a different name to that specific `AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D`, makes the error go away.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3530222925/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3530298084","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109257#issuecomment-3530298084","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109257","id":3530298084,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SbBLk","user":{"login":"Amandella27","id":112986970,"node_id":"U_kgDOBrwLWg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112986970?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amandella27","html_url":"https://github.com/Amandella27","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amandella27/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amandella27/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amandella27/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amandella27/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amandella27/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amandella27/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amandella27/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amandella27/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amandella27/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T00:29:16Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T00:40:07Z","body":"Hey just wanted to say that in our case we ended up having to open up every scene that had an animation tree node in it after migrating to 4.5. Once we found the problem scene, after opening it once and saving it, the error went away.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3530298084/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3662885020","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109257#issuecomment-3662885020","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109257","id":3662885020,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aUzCc","user":{"login":"byteseb","id":85042318,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDQyMzE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85042318?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/byteseb","html_url":"https://github.com/byteseb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/byteseb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/byteseb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/byteseb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/byteseb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/byteseb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/byteseb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/byteseb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/byteseb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/byteseb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-16T23:33:36Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T23:33:36Z","body":"This error starting happening to me in 4.5.1 when I reorganized the player's AnimationTree to contain smaller BlendTrees for each complex branch. \n\nSo I have an idle, walk, sprint, shoot and other BlendTrees saved as their own resource in the filesystem. I wanted to reuse them across different characters.\n\nThe player and enemy AnimationTrees have their own root nodes, but share these subtrees.\n\nI didn't have problems when I only had the player in the scene. But adding enemies caused the errors to show up when loading the scene with all characters and in the editor too.\n\nWhat fixed it for me was making all animation nodes local_to_scene. Of course, that would be a lot of manual work for a complex setup, so I used a tool script to do it and the error disappeared in the scene and editor.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3662885020/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3799521330","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109257#issuecomment-3799521330","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109257","id":3799521330,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ieBgy","user":{"login":"azuresu","id":35944559,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1OTQ0NTU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35944559?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuresu","html_url":"https://github.com/azuresu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuresu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuresu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuresu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuresu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuresu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuresu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuresu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuresu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuresu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T13:07:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T13:07:15Z","body":"Just want to report I had same issue (and animation is broken) when my character was instantiated from script. If I instantiate it in the editor, issue is gone.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3799521330/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3937567655","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109257#issuecomment-3937567655","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109257","id":3937567655,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qsoOn","user":{"login":"jondecko","id":476710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NjcxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/476710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jondecko","html_url":"https://github.com/jondecko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jondecko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jondecko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jondecko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jondecko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jondecko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jondecko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jondecko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jondecko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jondecko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T23:06:30Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T23:06:30Z","body":"Ran into this in my project (multiplayer, many NPC instances sharing the same `AnimationNodeStateMachine`). I was getting a ton of `Type mismatch between initial and final value: float and bool` errors per second in export builds, enough to produce multi-GB log files pretty quickly. Editor/F5 mode was totally clean.\n\nFirst thing I tried was setting `resource_local_to_scene = true` on the `AnimationNodeStateMachine`. This fixed exports completely, but then editor/F5 started producing the exact same errors that exports had before. Swapped which mode was broken.\n\nMy best guess is that `resource_local_to_scene` only duplicates the top-level state machine, not the child `AnimationNodeAnimation`/`Transition` sub-resources inside it. So you end up with multiple duplicated state machines still sharing the same child nodes, which might actually make the cache contamination worse rather than better.\n\nWhat ended up working in both editor and export builds was a programmatic deep duplicate in my setup code:\n\n```gdscript\nanimation_tree.active = false\nif animation_tree.tree_root:\n    animation_tree.tree_root = animation_tree.tree_root.duplicate(true)\nanimation_tree.anim_player = animation_tree.get_path_to(animation_player)\nanimation_tree.active = true\n```\n\nThe `duplicate(true)` deep-copies the entire hierarchy so each instance gets fully independent resources. Combined with deactivating the tree before rewiring `anim_player`, this eliminated the errors in both modes.\n\nNot sure if the editor vs export difference in behavior is expected or a separate issue. It seems like they handle sub-resource sharing differently at load time. Just sharing in case it helps anyone else hitting this.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3937567655/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]